$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Acetalization Procedure To a
well-stirred suspension of K 10 montmorillonite clay (190 mg) in dry
methanol (4 ml), trimethyl orthoformate (3 ml) and p-TsOH (10 mg) were
added successively, at room temperature. After 5 min, ketone (1 g) neat
or dissolved in the minimal amount of dry methanol or a dry inert solvent
such as hexane, dichloromethane, 1,2-dichloroethane, or nitromethane was
added. The mixture was stirred at room temperature for the specified
time, and the reaction was monitored by TLC or GC. Montmorillonite was
removed by filtration and washed with dichloromethane. The filtrate was
successively washed with saturated Na2CO3 solution and water and dried
over anhydrous MgSO4. The solvent was evaporated in vacuo. The pure
products were obtained from the crude by crystallization or
chromatography over silica gel or neutral alumina with mixtures of
hexane-EtOAc as eluents. Montmorillonite K 10 could be recovered and
reused by washing with distilled water and then with methanol and drying
overnight at 130°C. All the products were characterized by 1H NMR, 13C
NMR, and mass spectral analysis. Benzylideneacetophenone dimethyl acetal:
White crystals (CH2Cl2 - hexane), yield 97%. mp 42-43°C; 1H NMR δ: 7.84
(d, J = 7.8 Hz, 2H), 7.34-7.08 (m, 10H), 6.26 (d, J = 15.8 Hz, 1H), 3.23
(s, 6H); 13C NMR δ: 141.5, 136.7, 131.5, 131.1, 128.6, 128.4, 128.2,
127.7, 127.3, 127.0, 101.8, 49.0; MS m/z (%): 254 (M+, 69), 223 (M+ -
OMe, 100).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Simple method for the preparation of dimethyl acetals from ketones with
montmorillonite K 10 and p-toluenesulfonic acid
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Regas, David
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2006), 36(15), 2195-2201

