$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Acetals 1-4 and 6; General Procedure10 The
aldehyde (1 equiv) and the corresponding trialkyl orthoformate (1 to 1.5
equiv) were mixed in a flask containing APTS (p-TsOH·H2O, 0.002 equiv).
The mixture was stirred overnight at r.t., then directly distilled under
reduced pressure to yield the acetal. 1-(3,3-Dimethoxypropyl)benzene (1)
From 2-phenylpropionaldehyde (20 mL, 151 mmol), trimethyl orthoformate
(25 mL, 229 mmol) and APTS (57 mg, 0.3 mmol); yield: 26.1 g (96%);
colorless oil. bp 114 °C/15 Torr. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.16-7.31
(m, 5 H), 4.37 (t, 1 H, J = 6 Hz), 3.34 (s, 6 H), 2.68 (t, 2 H, J = 8
Hz), 1.93 (td, 2 H, J = 6, 8 Hz). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 141.6,
128.4, 128.3, 125.9, 103.7, 52.7, 34.0, 30.8.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Iron(III) chloride catalysis of the acetal-ene reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
