$DATUM Method B: To a solution of carbonyl compound 1 (5 mmol), (EtO)3CH
(7.5-12.5 mmol), in absolute ethanol (15 mL), NBS (0.05-0.10 mmol) was
added and the resulting solution was stirred at room temperature. After
completion of the reaction (TLC or GC), a cold aqueous solution of NaOH
(10%, 25 mL) was added and the mixture was extracted with Et2O (3 × 50
mL). The organic extracts were washed with water (3 ×25 mL) and dried
over anhydrous Na2SO4. Evaporation of the solvent under reduced pressure
gave almost pure product(s). Further purification was proceeded by vacuum
distillation to afford pure diethyl acetals 2 in good to excellent yields
(Table). Table Acelalization of Carbonyl Compounds with (EtO)3CH and NBS
under Almost Neutral Reaction Conditions Entry 11 Yield 96%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM using CH2Cl2/solvent gave 95% yield but took much longer
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM N-bromosuccinimide (NBS) as a powerful and chemoselective catalyst for
acetalization of carbonyl compounds under almost neutral reaction
conditions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Karimi, Babak; Seradj, Hassan; Ebrahimian, Gholam-Reza
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (1999), (9), 1456-1458

