$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Preparation of 1,3-Dioxanes via In-situ
Transacetalization; General Procedure: To a solution of carbonyl compound
1 (5 mmol), 1,3-propanediol (7.5-10 mmol), and (EtO)3CH (5 mmol) in dry
CH2Cl2 (15 mL), WCl6 (0.05-0.15 mmol) was added and the resulting
solution was stirred at room temperature. The progress of the reaction
was monitored by TLC or GC. After completion (Table 1), the reaction was
quenched with a cooled aqueous solution of NaOH (10%, 25 mL) and the
organic layer was separated and the residue was extracted with CH2Cl2 (3
x 30 mL). The organic extracts was washed with water (3 x35 mL), and
dried over anhydrous Na2SO4. Evaporation of the solvent under reduced
pressure gave almost pure 1,3-dioxane 3. Further purification was
achieved by vacuum distillation or recrystallization from the appropriate
solvent to give pure product(s) in good to excellent yields (Table 2).
3c, yield 96%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Tungsten hexachloride (WCl6), a highly efficient and chemoselective
catalyst for acetalization of carbonyl compounds
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Firouzabadi, H.; Iranpoor, N.; Karimi, B.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (1999), 29(13), 2255-2263

