$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Acetalization Procedure To a well-stirred suspension of K 10
montmorillonite clay (190 mg) in dry methanol (4 ml), trimethyl
orthoformate (3 ml) and p-TsOH (10 mg) were added successively, at room
temperature. After 5 min, ketone (1 g) neat or dissolved in the minimal
amount of dry methanol or a dry inert solvent such as hexane,
dichloromethane, 1,2-dichloroethane, or nitromethane was added. The
mixture was stirred at room temperature for the specified time, and the
reaction was monitored by TLC or GC. Montmorillonite was removed by
filtration and washed with dichloromethane. The filtrate was successively
washed with saturated Na2CO3 solution and water and dried over anhydrous
MgSO4. The solvent was evaporated in vacuo. The pure products were
obtained from the crude by crystallization or chromatography over silica
gel or neutral alumina with mixtures of hexane-EtOAc as eluents.
Montmorillonite K 10 could be recovered and reused by washing with
distilled water and then with methanol and drying overnight at 130°C. All
the products were characterized by 1H NMR, 13C NMR, and mass spectral
analysis. Table 1, entry 1, yield 96%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Simple method for the preparation of dimethyl acetals from ketones with
montmorillonite K 10 and p-toluenesulfonic acid
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Regas, David
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2006), 36(15), 2195-2201

