$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1,2-Propileneglycolacetals of 3-alkoxy-4-acyloxy-benzaldehydes
(IIIa-IIIf) and (IVa-IVf). 3-Alkoxy-4-acyloxybenzaldehyde (I), 0.01 mol,
1,2-propyleneglycol (II), 0.02 mol, FIBAN K-1 sulfonic cation-exchange
resin, 0.01 g, and benzene, 75 ml, were placed in a 100 ml single-neck
round-bottom fl ask supplied with a Dean- Stark attachment and a reflux
condenser. The mixture was boiled within 12-14 h with controlling
reaction completeness by the amount of water collected in the Dean-Stark
attachment (about 0.2 ml), the sulfonic cation-exchange resin was
separated by filtration through a glass porous filter, the benzene
solution was washed out with water to remove excess of
1,2-propyleneglycol (II) and with a saturated aqueous solution of sodium
chloride. After removal of benzene by vacuum distillation the target
products, compounds IIIa-IIIf and IVa-IVf, were obtained. Compound IIIa,
yield 96%. d20 20: 1.207; nD20°: 1.5454; Found, %: С 63.06; Н 6.75;
Formula: C13Н16O5; Calculated, %: С 61.89; Н 6.39.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM azeotropic removal of water, FIBAN K1 sulfonic cation-exchange resin
used, Dean-Stark apparatus used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Preparative synthesis of 1,2-propylene glycol acetals of
3-alkoxy-4-acyloxybenzaldehydes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Beresnevich, L. B.; Moiseichuk, K. L.; Zhukovskaya, N. A.; Dikusar, E. A.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Russian Journal of Applied Chemistry (2010), 83(5), 929-931

