$DATUM silica-bound
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 71-43-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A mixture of carbonyl compound (1, 2.00 mmol), pentaerythritol (2, 1.25
mmol), and silica sulfate (100 mg) were mixed and treated under microwave
irradiation 30-300 sec (Table 1). The progress of the reaction was
monitored by TLC. After completion of the reaction, the mixture was
cooled, CH2Cl2 (15 mL) was added to the reaction mixture and the catalyst
was filtered off. The catalyst was washed with CH2Cl2 (5 mL x 3).
Evaporation of the solvent under reduced pressure afforded the crude
product. The crude product was purified by column chromatography on
silica gel or recrystallized to give diacetals 3. Selected spectral data
of some of the products are given below: 3a, yield 96% Mp (°C) Found:
43-44; Reported: 43-44[8] νmax (cm-1) 2960, 2932, 2872, 1160, 1114, 1078,
994, 724; δH 0.90 [6H, t, J= 6.1 Hz, 2 x (CH3)], 1.20-1.70 [8H, m, 2 x
(CH2)2], 3.25-3.70 (6H, m, Heq, Hax), 4.40 [2H, t, J= 4.4 Hz, 2 x (CH)].
4.65 (2H, d, J= 11.4Hz, Heq).
