$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Acetalization of 14a; Conversion of 14a to 14c. A mixture of dione 14a
(30 mg, 0.08 mmol), 2,2-dimethylpropane- 1,3-diol (25 mg, 0.24 mmol),
PTSA (3 mg), and benzene (10 mL) was refluxed for 12 h with a Dean-Stark
water separator. Usual workup and removal of solvent furnished a residue,
which was purified by column chromatography using silica gel. Elution
with 35% ethyl acetate-hexane. Mono-acetal 14c (35 mg, 95%). This sample
was found to be identical (mp, IR, and 1H NMR) to the sample 14c derived
from mono-acetal 4c. 14c: mp 190-191 °C; IR (KBr) 1748, 1709, 1281, 1119
cm-1; 1H NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.70-6.59 (2H, m), 4.34 (1H, d, J = 4.5
Hz), 3.94 (1H, d, J = 4.5 Hz), 3.80 (3H, s), 3.69 (3H, s), 3.67 (1H, d, J
= 9.3 Hz), 3.43-3.31 (4H, m), 2.62-2.57 (2H, m), 2.45 (1H, t, J = 6 Hz),
2.33 (1H, dd, J 1 = 10 Hz, J 2 = 2 Hz), 2.12 (1H, t, J = 6.5 Hz), 1.77
(1H, 1/2 ABq, J = 10.8 Hz), 1.52 (1H, 1/2 ABq, J = 10.9 Hz), 1.05 (3H,
s), 0.70 (3H, s); 13C NMR (50 MHz, CDCl3) δ 211.2, 166.7, 165.5, 144.2,
142.1, 135.9, 135.2, 102.8, 73.2, 70.8, 60.7, 54.8, 52.1, 51.7, 49.6,
46.6, 43.8, 43.3, 42.0, 39.7, 39.3, 39.1, 38.4, 29.5, 23.4, 22.5. Anal.
Calcd for C26H28O7: C, 69.01; H, 6.24. Found: C, 69.12; H, 6.28.
